# The exact `wolf --version` string that commit produces (first line; the
# binary also prints a second line naming its lupin pairing — 0.1.36 at this
# pin, up from 0.1.34 at v0.2.12). `lspconf doctor` fails on a mismatch: a
# stale local `wolf` producing green transcripts is the failure mode the pin
# exists to prevent.
#
# D57 decides the shape. A build is a release build only when the builder
# stamps BOTH `WOLF_COMMIT=<short sha>` and `WOLF_RELEASE=v{crate version}`,
# and the second is granted only when that exact tag points at HEAD. This pin
# is at v0.2.14, so a release build prints the BARE version and the pin clause.
# An unstamped build still prints `+dev.unknown` — the string any trunk build
# of the same crate version prints, which is exactly the stale-binary hole —
# so the pinned string remains a stamped build's, and `cargo xtask dist` in
# the submodule is the builder that computes the stamp (README §Running the
# server lane locally; its plain-cargo recipe cannot grant the release half).
#
# `xtask compat`'s `version_number` reads the number out of this string; it
# learned semver build metadata at le03 and takes the bare tag form
# unchanged — `0.2.14`, no `+` to strip. Asserted in xtask/src/compat.rs.
#
# SEVEN HEX DIGITS FOR THE SIXTH PIN RUNNING, and the line below was READ OFF
# THE ACQUIRED ARTIFACT rather than off any clone on this box — the darwin
# arm64 archive of release 388081784, sha256
# 80407e31b89cae684163fd9fd79c3935a5fe63873dcb16376c36c8596af61b54 (the
# release asset's own digest, matched after download), whose `wolf --version`
# prints exactly the string below. That matters because wolf-lang#199 is still
# open: D57's pin clause is clone-dependent, `git rev-parse --short` sizes its
# AUTO abbreviation to the PACKED object count of the clone it runs in, and the
# step is at 16,384 packed objects (2^14) — measured at le08 against three
# scratch repositories answering 7 / 8 / 8 hex digits (git 2.50.1). A locally
# built submodule binary on a big clone can therefore print eight digits and
# fail `doctor` here, and that refusal is the pin doing its job. The remedy is
# upstream — `--short=7`, or `core.abbrev`, in whatever computes the stamp.
# See docs/COMPAT.md.
